<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Plan of Saint Gall</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 820</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Plan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-gall">Saint Gall</a> is a drawing of an ideal Benedictine monastery made around 820 at Reichenau Abbey and sent to Abbot Gozbert of Saint Gall. Drawn on five sewn sheets of parchment, it shows a church, cloister and some forty other buildings, including workshops, gardens and an infirmary. It is the only surviving major architectural drawing from the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> and is kept in the Abbey Library of Saint Gall.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/plan-of-saint-gall.jpg" alt="Plan of Saint Gall" width="320" height="465" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Codex_Sangallensis_1092_recto.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
